1
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:03,375
Has this ever happened to you?

2
00:00:03,390 --> 00:00:04,875
You bought something online.

3
00:00:04,890 --> 00:00:06,135
You were unhappy with it

4
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:07,180
and requested a return.

5
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:08,895
Then the store told you:

6
00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:09,915
Your refund is approved.

7
00:00:09,930 --> 00:00:11,800
You do not need to send it back.

8
00:00:12,030 --> 00:00:12,615
Wait a moment!

9
00:00:12,630 --> 00:00:14,020
Is the store really that generous?

10
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:15,915
It may not be generosity.

11
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:17,860
The store may have done the math.

12
00:00:18,030 --> 00:00:20,020
Here are two business concepts.

13
00:00:20,130 --> 00:00:21,940
Reverse Logistics

14
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:23,115
Reverse Logistics

15
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:23,535
And

16
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:24,765
Cost-to-Serve

17
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:25,780
Cost-to-Serve

18
00:00:26,010 --> 00:00:27,045
Let us work it out.

19
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:28,900
All these figures are hypothetical.

20
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:31,240
An item sells for $20.

21
00:00:31,290 --> 00:00:33,195
The customer requests a full refund.

22
00:00:33,210 --> 00:00:34,875
If the store asks for a return

23
00:00:34,890 --> 00:00:37,275
return shipping costs $6.

24
00:00:37,290 --> 00:00:39,820
Inspection and handling cost another $3.

25
00:00:40,470 --> 00:00:41,655
After the item comes back

26
00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:43,575
assume its recovery value is only $5.

27
00:00:43,590 --> 00:00:46,420
The recovered item is worth $5.

28
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:48,820
But processing the return costs $9.

29
00:00:48,870 --> 00:00:49,575
Five minus nine

30
00:00:49,590 --> 00:00:50,920
equals negative four dollars.

31
00:00:51,030 --> 00:00:51,855
In other words

32
00:00:51,870 --> 00:00:54,580
asking for a return loses $4 more.

33
00:00:55,650 --> 00:00:58,060
So for some low-value products

34
00:00:58,170 --> 00:00:59,355
the store may choose

35
00:00:59,370 --> 00:01:01,180
to refund without a return.

36
00:01:01,530 --> 00:01:04,480
This avoids extra reverse logistics costs.

37
00:01:04,710 --> 00:01:07,120
But this is not right for every item.

38
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:09,075
For a higher-value item

39
00:01:09,090 --> 00:01:10,815
or one that can be resold

40
00:01:10,830 --> 00:01:12,520
a return may make more sense.

41
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:14,595
So next time a store says

42
00:01:14,610 --> 00:01:15,975
you can keep the item

43
00:01:15,990 --> 00:01:16,815
you will know

44
00:01:16,830 --> 00:01:18,795
it may not be generosity.

45
00:01:18,810 --> 00:01:20,260
It may be a cost calculation.

46
00:01:20,670 --> 00:01:21,615
Business decisions

47
00:01:21,630 --> 00:01:23,715
are sometimes less about earning more

48
00:01:23,730 --> 00:01:26,320
and more about losing less.

49
00:01:26,430 --> 00:01:28,300
This is Business Through Data.
